<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shiraz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shiraz is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, known for its gardens and poets such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafez">Hafez</a> and Saadi. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a> made it the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a> and adorned it with mosques, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bazaar">bazaars</a> and a citadel. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> leader Agha Mohammad Khan captured the city in the 1790s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shiraz.jpg" alt="Shiraz" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: آرش (Arche) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Darvaze_Ghoran11.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
